      "severity": "high",
      "summary": "Migration extraction leaves duplicate executable definitions in the legacy registry module",
      "details": "S05-T01 is required to provide task-owned migration implementation inputs and runtime extraction of historical S00/S01 executable definitions. The runtime specs and impls now import S00/S01 component migrations from task-owned implementation modules, but packages/convex/confect/internal/migrations.ts still contains the same executable componentMigrations.define bodies for probe.expand/probe.fail and stableTenant organization/workspace expansion. The focused test only checks for the new imports and a couple of import-string absences, so it can pass while the old executable definitions remain as a second source of truth. This leaves future registry generation/cleanup ambiguous and requires task rework to complete the extraction or otherwise remove the duplicated executable definitions from the lane-owned source boundary.",
